- On 2026-10-01 the user reopened CHG-0030 for English: the previous English exclusion left B03/B07 text visibly low. An EN-only 12-source-px shift now centers both visible lines while preserving rings and non-EN styles; Pro/Pro Max before/after WebKit images and 8/8 focused EN/RU interaction and ink tests pass, plus 2/2 EN production WebKit checks on refreshed `:3020`. Type/lint/build pass and independent visual/behavior audit passes. Native review/final gate remain pending under the user's short timebox; CHG-0030 remains OPEN until then.
- [CHG-0034](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0034) constrains all six Confidence Document cards: translated title/detail text wraps inside a shrinkable grid column, long RU/DE/FR/ES headings use local size adjustments, and footer labels and arrows share a centered action row. EN source composition and RU/AR Pro/Pro Max screenshots were checked; production WebKit matrix covers 330/330 card/locale/width states with zero overflow. RU/AR document dialog actions pass in mobile/desktop browsers, and the full production suite passes 49 tests with 15 expected skips. Scoped native review of this fix has no remaining actionable finding; independent scope, visual, behavior and review/performance gates passed.
- The font/button visual and behavior gates passed independent audit. Pro comparisons cover all eight page bands and all 14 CTAs; Pro Max is responsive evidence. Tight pill crop differences remain 8.50–12.93% (threshold 0.15), mainly rim/glyph rendering; no pixel-perfect claim. The prior FAQ “tint difference” disposition was wrong: duplicated source/CSS surfaces and vertical drift were material defects, subsequently reopened for correction; see [FAQ fix](docs/fix-faq-accordion.md). Source decorative feature pictograms remain outside the font/button correction. English assets cannot establish native-script editorial accuracy or BankGothic embedding rights.
- Latest typecheck, lint, production build and **24/24 browser tests** passed on Pro/Pro Max WebKit and desktop Chromium/Firefox. The localized-button matrix covers 14 CTAs × 11 locales × 375/402/440/768/1440 CSS px: 770/770 states with exactly one visual text line, adequate internal margins/arrow clearance and no canvas overflow. Hero and comparison CTA dialog interactions passed in all 11 locales. Earlier checks covered all 24 modal actions per primary device, expanded pill hit areas, Arabic, keyboard focus containment/restoration and Escape. Native reviews found and prompted fixes for standalone calibration and system font fallback; final native review found no actionable defect. Its sandbox could not run fresh WebKit, so main-session production browser evidence supplies that check. See [localized fix evidence](docs/fix-localized-buttons.md) and [implementation verification](docs/font-button-implementation-2026-09-30.md).
- Latest production FAQ-flow check: Chromium402×874 DPR3,4×CPU, unthrottled loopback. Cold FCP/LCP244ms, CLS0;1,188,991B transferred (151,430B JS,256,343B fonts); warm LCP60ms. Normal-CPU162-frame scroll p95 17.6ms, none >33ms. No INP/Lighthouse claim. See [FAQ background evidence](docs/fix-faq-background.md).
- CHG-0026/0027: closed FAQ remains source-aligned with −; independently open rows show ×. Answers now grow the document, shifting all suffix artwork/text/targets together without a nested scroller or extra client JS. The prior expanded-side-gutter/central-gradient background was rejected by the user: it changed gaps/corners. CHG-0027 was reopened and is now technically approved after correction: full-width row crops preserve corners/gaps and the native card surface, extending only an opened row’s middle. Pro/Max/Arabic visual audit,16 locale/width cases and16 browser tests passed; final native review found no actionable defect and auditor closeout passed. CHG-0026 retains technical approval; CHG-0027’s earlier approval was superseded; the new background fix passed independent final audit; user acceptance remains NOT_RECORDED. The source-scaled grid splits at Y27147/Y28207. See [current FAQ background correction](docs/fix-faq-background.md) and the [historical flow fix](docs/fix-faq-flow.md). The outer artwork seam CHG-0014 and cursor investigation CHG-0025 remain open; feature pictograms CHG-0015 were subsequently corrected in CHG-0044/0045 and remain `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED` pending native review.
- The implemented site is committed on `main`; `5727804` was the latest site commit before the right-edge artwork correction. Preserve user files and unrelated changes. No project Codex hooks are configured; stage auditing uses the profile and [docs/supervision.md](docs/supervision.md).
- CHG-0041 corrects the intermittent white line along the right edge of the long background. The source PNG's x=940 column is transparent at Y221–1896, 2854–3264, 5043–11469 and had been flattened to white in WebP. Only derived tiles `00.webp`–`04.webp` were regenerated with neighboring opaque pixels; source references, CSS and layout geometry remain unchanged. Pro/Max WebKit and desktop Chromium screenshots and nine scroll positions per profile show no white edge; four changed tile joins were inspected. The independent visual/adaptation audit passed; user acceptance is `NOT_RECORDED`. See [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0041) and [lesson](LESSONS.md#check-the-outer-pixels-of-derived-artwork).
- CHG-0042 addresses blank artwork during fast scroll/cold load and mid-page locale transitions. Production tests on Pro/Pro Max WebKit and desktop Chromium pass 12/12 focused image/locale/stalled-resource cases; the switcher regression passes 14 applicable cases. The first new RU/AR frame retains y=6500 and decoded shared artwork. A local Chromium 402×874/DPR3 sample measured LCP160ms, CLS0, 2.82MB resources, 12/12 art images loaded and scroll p95 16.8ms/0 frames over33ms; no Lighthouse or INP claim. Native `/review` was blocked by automatic approval review because it would export the private uncommitted diff; that gate remains unpassed. See [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0042) and [lesson](LESSONS.md#test-fast-travel-and-cold-reload-before-approving-long-artwork-delivery).
- CHG-0028 adds a user-requested back-to-top control absent from the original render. A small client component appears after scrolling, stays at the lower-right safe area, adapts visually over light/dark artwork, returns keyboard/touch users to the top, and has labels in all 11 locales. Final 20/20 browser checks, Pro/Pro Max and responsive screenshots, production build/type/lint, native follow-up review, and independent visual/behavior/performance gates pass. The final journal audit found stale pending wording; it was corrected before delivery. See [feature record](docs/back-to-top.md) and `screenshots/actual/back-to-top/`. This addition does not claim a render pixel match because the source has no corresponding control.
- CHG-0043 is the later user correction to that supplemental button's position: its phone-only 72px bottom minimum was removed. Pro/Pro Max production WebKit now measure a 20px bottom gap in emulation, with safe-area handling retained for real devices; focused behavior tests pass 3/3. Native review of this latest one-line CSS correction is blocked by automatic approval review, so CHG-0043 remains `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`.
- CHG-0044 replaces the four wrong Unicode feature marks (control, draw, intensity, session) and restores three source dividers using transparent pixel extractions from `background_text.png` over `background.png`. The source reconstruction misses zero changed pixels in those bands; Pro/Pro Max/Arabic/desktop screenshots and 44 locale/width states passed, as did 3 focused tests and type/lint/build. Native review remains blocked by automatic approval review, so this change is `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`; see [source map](docs/feature-icon-map.md).
- CHG-0045 subsequently replaces the seven wrong technology glyphs and their straight CSS connectors with source-derived gold forms, bent routes and terminal dots. Pro aligned source and browser crops, Pro Max, Arabic and desktop were inspected; 3 new and 6 existing browser tests, 44/44 locale/width states, source reconstruction and type/lint/build passed. One local Chromium run measured LCP124ms, CLS0 and 63KB transferred for the seven images; no INP/Lighthouse claim. Native review remains blocked by automatic approval review, so CHG-0045 and umbrella CHG-0015 are `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`. See [technology map](docs/technology-icon-map.md) and saved evidence in `screenshots/actual/technology-icons/`.
- On 2026-10-03 CHG-0049 supersedes only the icon **shapes** in CHG-0044/0045 with the designer's `design/assets/ICON_Kit/` PNGs. [Elements Mapping](docs/elements-mapping.md) maps 12 files to 11 unique rendered icons (I06 duplicates I05); `lib/icon-map.json` drives the live IDs. The original three dividers and seven connector paths are separate derived layers. A uniform 28-source-px lift and the next individual placement were rejected by the customer as too high. The six-icon target, initially provisional, lowers I01/I03/I04/I05/I07/I08 another 4–6 source px; I02 Smart Core is held unchanged because the customer asked for six of seven visible icons without specifying which to exclude. A later correction centers all seven technology icons over their translated label axes outside English, keeping Y, English X, connectors and I09–I12 fixed; [154-pair Pro/Pro Max evidence](docs/evidence/icon-centering/geometry.json) and DE/AR/EN screenshots show no translated center drift. The customer later explicitly accepted the current vertical distance, resolving the earlier six-of-seven selection blocker for the visible result; the integrated correction is technically VERIFIED. Older technical passes remain historical for rejected positions. CHG-0048 was still open at that stage; CHG-0056 resolved it on 2026-10-04.
- CHG-0055 corrects the remaining **English** Light & Sound center: I05 now uses target X706 instead of original X711 in the 941px source coordinate system, placing its 28px box center on the text axis720. Non-English `localizedX736`, Y/size/PNG and all other icons stay unchanged. Production WebKit Pro/Max EN/DE/AR geometry is within 0.008 normalized CSS px of the label axis; eight focused browser tests, assembled-section screenshots, build/type/lint and native review pass. See [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0055) and [evidence](docs/evidence/light-axis/).
- CHG-0050: Firefox locale-switcher test twice failed because it called `decode()` during a changing lazy-image request. It now polls for **all visible tiles** to be loaded; the final full suite passed 78/18, and its strengthened scenario passed 4/4 browser profiles. The test sync defect and prevention are recorded separately from the icon correction.
- CHG-0051: The Freedom of Choice subtitle alone now uses warm dark brown `#41342d` for stronger readability. Production WebKit Pro/Pro Max screenshots and 22 locale×device checks showed the expected color without overflow; type/lint/build passed. The later CHG-0049 acceptance and horizontal correction are verified separately from this subtitle change.
- CHG-0052 restores the source luminous arcs and glints around the PRO/GOLD comparison block as a masked 700×400 transparent layer derived from `background_text.png` while keeping text and B08 live and translated. It is lazy-loaded near the section: zero wave requests on the first viewport and one decoded request after a fast jump. Real WebKit Pro/Max/DE/AR crops and an 11-locale contact sheet were inspected; the 4-profile browser spec checks all locale centers, overflow and Arabic B08 behavior. Build/type/lint, 10-stop assembled scroll and final native review pass; the independent stage gates passed. [Map](docs/expression-waves-map.md), [evidence](docs/evidence/expression-waves/), [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0052). CHG-0048 was still open at that stage; CHG-0056 resolved it on 2026-10-04.

CHG-0024 originally restored scroll chaining; CHG-0027 subsequently removes the nested FAQ scroller entirely. Wheel injection uses desktop input mode for WebKit because mobile WebKit does not support it; actual mobile screenshots/interaction checks remain separate. Historical [scroll evidence](docs/fix-faq-scroll.md) is retained.

## Approved supplemental render correction

- `design/references/fix_RAMSIDER_BUSINESS.png` supplements the main render with **RAMSIDER Business** above the second account card subtitle. Implemented as translation key `businessAccount` / `#business-account-title`, using Open Sans Regular and the adjacent account-heading style; the branded name is invariant across locales. The card's accessible name includes it. Pro/Pro Max and Arabic crops, 15 locale/width/action checks, type/lint/build and focused native review passed. See [fix record](docs/fix-ramsider-business.md). This newer screenshot takes precedence only for this addition; source renders remain intact.
- On 2026-10-01 the customer corrected the [current switcher specification](design/references/locale-switcher/README.md) (CHG-0046): the bare flag + uppercase two-letter code + chevron belongs to the header and scrolls away with it. Flag and code are 1.5× smaller than the rejected first implementation, the chevron slightly smaller, and code/chevron remain black. The old scroll contrast map and handler were removed. The existing light translucent 11-language dropdown and its selection logic remain. Corrected Pro/Pro Max WebKit and desktop production checks passed 14 applicable tests, with 18 profile-specific skips; native review found no actionable regression. The active `:3020` preview was restarted and checked. The earlier 20 PASS result applies only to the rejected fixed version. The old PNGs remain in `design/archive/locale-switcher-2026-09-30/` as historical source. The original product art and copy are still governed by the main references. Platform emoji appearance varies. An unrelated missing favicon remains open as CHG-0035.
- CHG-0053 is verified: only the closed switcher's two-letter code is optically aligned to the flag. The smooth formula includes a small mobile compensation (0.4px, JA 0.8px), a 500–700px midline adjustment, and a separate JA correction. The final 176-state WebKit/Chromium matrix across 11 locales and eight widths measures painted-center offsets within -1.25..+1 CSS px; another 22 checks at the user's actual 756px/DPR2 IAB width measure -0.75..+0.25 CSS px. Locale tests pass 12 applicable checks with 12 intended skips; production `:3020` serves the final CSS. Native review raised an unrelated, source-disproven CHG-0052 mask concern; independent auditor passed all CHG-0053 gates. See [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0053). The dropdown remains as specified in CHG-0036.
- CHG-0054 makes the navigation dropdown use the locale dropdown's exact light translucent glass, gold rim, blur and shadow; a faint link text shadow keeps it readable over the hero. Outside pointer input and page scroll close the menu; internal list scroll, Escape, hash links, keyboard focus and locale-menu exclusivity remain functional. Pro/Pro Max WebKit, desktop Chromium/Firefox, Arabic and all 11 navigation translations were checked; `:3020` was rebuilt/restarted and smoke-tested. See [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0054) and [evidence](docs/evidence/nav-menu/). The locale dropdown itself was not changed.
- [CHG-0036](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0036) remains the current dropdown design: light `rgb(250 247 242 / .45)` panel, dark names, fine gold rim, 112px width, no checkmark and highlighted current row. The earlier graphite panel and [CHG-0037](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0037) capsule alignment/scrolled relocation are historical closed-control states, superseded by CHG-0046. The old [follow-up report](docs/locale-switcher-follow-up-2026-10-01.md) retains its original dropdown evidence. Separate favicon CHG-0035 and absolute scroll restoration CHG-0038 remain open.
- On 2026-10-01, the user's active `:3020` production preview was found serving an older CSS build despite the verified CHG-0036/0037 source. It was rebuilt and restarted; fresh live screenshots show the translucent gold-rimmed menu and desktop header centers within 1.5 CSS px. Addressed preview tests passed (3 applicable, 3 profile skips). The repeated report and root cause are appended to CHG-0036/0037; see the preview freshness lesson in [LESSONS.md](LESSONS.md). The `:3020` server remains the current preview; a later source change requires another build and restart.

## Demo video

On 2026-10-01 CHG-0039 produced an 89.50-second Playwright site demo at [`deliverables/ramsider-uno-demo.mp4`](deliverables/ramsider-uno-demo.mp4). It shows top-to-bottom scroll, 40/40 distinct planned controls, RU then EN copy, final back-to-top, an original English arena-style synthetic narration, crowd mix, and selectable English captions. Browser action audit and full MP4 decode pass; Pro Max shows no overflow. This is a recording of the current site, not user approval of CHG-0036. CHG-0039 remains `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`: model-side audio audition is unavailable and native review was rejected by automatic approval review because `--uncommitted` could send the whole repository diff externally. See [script and evidence](docs/demo-video-script.md) and [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0039).

## Open dependencies

The render does not supply confirmed prices, certificates/files, film media, FAQ answers, account/configurator/checkout services, or final action destinations. Local controls open explanatory modal dialogs instead of fabricated checkout or documents. All translated copy and product claims need product approval before publication. See [PRODUCT.md](PRODUCT.md) for specific claims and flows.

## Update rule

Update this file when a **verified** project state, durable decision, or external dependency changes, including during long work before context is lost. Replace stale entries instead of appending a running diary. Date material changes and link to the code, command, screenshot, or document that supports them. Check volatile claims against the current files; current user instructions and evidence win over stale memory. Label assumptions and unverified facts explicitly; keep secrets, private data, generated logs, and temporary task notes out. When a repeatable error or user correction yields a prevention rule, update [LESSONS.md](LESSONS.md) instead. Reconcile any affected topic document so the sources do not contradict each other.
